ROOT CAUSE (pre-existing, repo-wide, NOT this surface):
  The XcodeGen spec (apps/apple/project.yml) lists `TeslaSync/feature-views` and `TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets`
  as APP-target sources with no excludes, so all 71 sibling `*Tests.swift` files (BackendTool.Tests.swift,
  FleetApiSection.ModelTests.swift, every *Widget.Tests.swift, …) are compiled INTO the non-test app target,
  where `import XCTest` cannot resolve. The app build therefore fails on the first such sibling
  (BackendTool.Tests.swift) before linking — on BOTH platforms — independent of this surface (0 EnvironmentSlide
  errors in both logs). Fixing it requires routing `*Tests.swift` to the TeslaSyncTests / TeslaSync-macOSTests
  targets in apps/apple/project.yml — a file OUTSIDE this prompt's allowed scope (EnvironmentSlide.* only) and
  parallel-unsafe to edit from a surface slot (Honesty Covenant #7 "No predecessor bypass"). This matches the
  established precedent for every P4 feature-view surface (e.g. 0005 FleetTelemetryHealth, 0086): signed Xcode
  app build/test is DEFERRED to the integration runner; the surface is verified via host gates + both-SDK SDK
  compiles + executed projection/model tests. Evidence captured (not assumed): /tmp/tslogs/{ios-buildtest,
  macos-build}.log show the identical XCTest blocker with zero EnvironmentSlide diagnostics.

